# ==============================================================
# Mews environment — copy to .env and fill in the two tokens.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # then paste your Connector tokens into .env
#
# .env is gitignored. .env.example is committed and must NEVER
# contain a real value. Do not add tokens to this file.
# ==============================================================


# --------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRET — Connector API. Server-side only, never in a browser.
# --------------------------------------------------------------
# These are PROPERTY-WIDE credentials. Whoever holds them can read
# every guest profile and post charges to any folio. They are not
# scoped to an endpoint, a guest, or a date.
#
# Only server/springer-proxy.example.js reads these. Nothing in
# js/ ever sees them, and nothing in js/ ever should.
#
# Get them from: Mews Commander -> Integrations -> Connector API.

MEWS_CLIENT_TOKEN=
MEWS_ACCESS_TOKEN=


# --------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT SECRET — but kept server-side so the client never names a
# Connector host or spoofs the property.
# --------------------------------------------------------------
MEWS_CONNECTOR_BASE=https://api.mews-demo.com
MEWS_CLIENT=Cascadian Pavilion 1.0.0
MEWS_ENTERPRISE_ID=d73927b5-3500-43a6-9988-b409011e1672


# --------------------------------------------------------------
# Local proxy plumbing
# --------------------------------------------------------------
PORT=8787
ALLOWED_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8000


# ==============================================================
# PUBLIC values are NOT here — they live in js/config.js
# ==============================================================
# This is a static site with no build step, so the browser cannot
# read a .env file. Every value page JS needs is therefore in
# js/config.js, served to visitors, and public by design:
#
#   ENTERPRISE_ID                 d73927b5-3500-43a6-9988-b409011e1672
#   DISTRIBUTOR_CONFIGURATION_ID  602a440b-7c79-4b18-9b4e-b409011e18cc
#   CLIENT_NAME                   "My Client 1.0.0"  (allowlisted on demo)
#   SPRINGER_SERVICE_ID           fea4735d-7238-427f-bcf5-b4b7011f78ce
#   SPRINGER_TICKET_PRODUCT_ID    ff471e6c-ddfb-44f5-8da7-b4b701201e97
#
# Those are identifiers, not credentials. The Distributor API is
# anonymous by design and publishing them is expected.
#
# Two switches in js/config.js decide what touches the real property:
#   SPRINGER_LIVE_GUEST_LOOKUP    reads real reservations
#   SPRINGER_LIVE_CHARGE          WRITES a real order item to a real folio
#
#
# ==============================================================
# WHEN THIS MOVES TO LOVABLE — the split changes shape
# ==============================================================
# Lovable builds on Vite, which INLINES every VITE_-prefixed value
# into the client bundle at build time. That prefix is a publication
# marker, not access control:
#
#   VITE_ANYTHING   -> public, readable in View Source
#   no prefix       -> invisible to the frontend; Edge Functions only
#
# So in the Lovable project:
#
#   .env (committed as .env.example)   the public ids, VITE_-prefixed
#   Edge Function secrets              MEWS_CLIENT_TOKEN
#                                      MEWS_ACCESS_TOKEN
#                                      MEWS_CLIENT
#                                      MEWS_CONNECTOR_BASE
#                                      MEWS_ENTERPRISE_ID
#
# Set the secrets in Lovable -> Settings -> Secrets (or Supabase ->
# Edge Functions -> Secrets) and read them with Deno.env.get().
# NEVER as VITE_MEWS_ACCESS_TOKEN.
#
# Full mapping, tables and a porting order: "Lovable Context.md"
